Berlin Airlift's code is written fresh in TypeScript. What it carries over from VerdeNFC is behaviour the machine
requires byte for byte: the CRC16 single-use and multi-use and CRC8
checksum algorithms, the tag merge and write model, the pause stepping,
and the profile templates (originally collected by VerdeNFC from the
Bonaverde owner community, the Hackaverde group, Craig Whyte and
Michael Grundler).

The NFC tag layout and the published card dumps used as test vectors
come from hackaverde (PostalBlab and contributors):
https://github.com/PostalBlab/hackaverde

